# Phase 1 — Repository Finalization Contract Hardening

## Objective
Fix the final persistence consistency problem at the repository boundary.

## Main issue being solved
### Issue
Final TAT result persistence is split across separate writes/documents and the app can observe `COMPLETED` before the result is consumable.

### Problem caused
- Result screen sees `COMPLETED`
- `olqResult` is not yet fetchable/visible
- fallback fetch is required
- UI temporarily enters inconsistent state

## Proposed solution
Introduce a **single repository finalization contract** for TAT result completion.

### Design
Add a dedicated repository method, for example:
- `finalizeTATAnalysisResult(submissionId, olqResult, metadata)`

This method must:
1. Persist final result to `psych_results`
2. Persist final submission completion metadata to `submissions`
3. Only mark completion once final result persistence has succeeded
4. Return failure if any step fails

### Preferred persistence semantics
At minimum, submission metadata should include:
- `analysisStatus = COMPLETED`
- `resultUpdatedAt`
- optional `hasOlqResult = true`
- optional `resultSource = psych_results`

This keeps submission state self-describing even if the full result body is stored elsewhere.

### Architecture rationale
This keeps SSOT at the repository layer:
- workers don’t manually coordinate multi-step persistence
- all finalization logic lives in one place
- future test types can reuse the pattern

## Files likely involved
- `core/domain/src/main/kotlin/com/ssbmax/core/domain/repository/SubmissionRepository.kt`
- `core/data/src/main/kotlin/com/ssbmax/core/data/remote/TATSubmissionRepository.kt`
- `core/data/src/main/kotlin/com/ssbmax/core/data/remote/PsychTestSubmissionRepository.kt`
- `core/data/src/main/kotlin/com/ssbmax/core/data/remote/FirestoreSubmissionRepository.kt`

## TDD tasks
Write tests first:
### Unit tests
- finalization succeeds only when both persistence targets succeed
- completion metadata is not written on partial failure
- `userId` is preserved for Firestore rule compliance
- repository returns failure when `psych_results` write fails
- repository returns failure when submission metadata write fails

### Integration tests
- Firestore emulator or repository integration tests verifying:
  - final result is available before completion is observable as final
  - submission metadata is coherent after finalization

## Implementation tasks
- Add new repository method
- Refactor existing `updateTATOLQResult` callers to use the new method
- Keep old methods only if still used elsewhere; otherwise deprecate/remove to avoid ambiguity
- Update comments and names to reflect actual behavior

## Security checks
- Preserve Firestore security compatibility (`userId` on psych_results)
- No broadened write scope
- No leakage of story text or sensitive payloads in logs

## Validation gate
- Targeted repository unit tests
- Targeted repository integration tests
- `./gradlew :core:data:testDebugUnitTest`
- `./gradlew check`

## Exit criteria
- Final result persistence has one authoritative contract
- No more repository ambiguity about what “complete” means
- All tests/build green

