# Phase 2 — Worker Reliability and Explicit Failure Semantics

## Objective
Make worker success/failure reflect actual persistence success.

## Main issues being solved
### Issue 1
Workers ignore `Result<Unit>` returned by repository write methods.

### Problem caused
- silent persistence failures
- worker continues as if success occurred
- notifications/cache invalidation may run despite failed writes

### Issue 2
Notification and cache invalidation occur too loosely relative to persistence confirmation.

### Problem caused
- app may tell user results are ready before the final state is truly durable/consumable

## Proposed solution
Make `TATSynthesisWorker` fail-fast on repository failures and perform side effects only after verified finalization.

### Design
- Replace unchecked repository calls with explicit success handling:
  - `getOrThrow()` style or explicit branching
- Finalization sequence:
  1. finalize result in repository
  2. verify success
  3. invalidate dashboard cache
  4. send results-ready notification
- On failure:
  - retry if transient
  - mark failed only after retry exhaustion

## Files likely involved
- `app/src/main/kotlin/com/ssbmax/workers/TATSynthesisWorker.kt`
- possibly supporting helpers extracted from it to stay under 300 LOC

## TDD tasks
### Unit tests
- worker retries when repository finalization returns failure
- worker does not send notification when finalization fails
- worker does not invalidate cache when finalization fails
- worker marks failed only after retry exhaustion
- worker succeeds only after finalization succeeds

### Integration tests
- worker + fake repository + fake notification/cache collaborator tests
- if possible, WorkManager test harness with `TestListenableWorkerBuilder`

## Implementation tasks
- Refactor `TATSynthesisWorker` to explicit success/failure flow
- Extract helper functions/classes if needed to keep file size clean
- Ensure comments/logs match behavior

## Security checks
- Ensure no extra sensitive payloads are logged during failure handling
- Verify failure paths do not expose internal errors to UI unsafely

## Validation gate
- `./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest --tests "*TATSynthesisWorkerTest"`
- broader app unit tests
- `./gradlew check`

## Exit criteria
- Worker no longer assumes repository writes succeeded
- notification/cache invalidation are persistence-safe
- build/tests all green

