# Phase 5 — Partial-Assessment Transparency

## Objective
If synthesis completes using degraded evidence, make that explicit in domain and UI.

## Main issue being solved
### Issue
Synthesis can succeed with partial valid stories, but the result may look identical to a full-quality analysis.

### Problem caused
- misleading confidence
- reduced trust
- harder debugging/support conversations

## Proposed solution
Add explicit degradation metadata to the final TAT analysis result model and display logic.

### Recommended metadata
- `validStoriesCount`
- `failedStoriesCount`
- `usedPartialAssessment`
- optional `analysisNotice` or `analysisWarnings`

### UI behavior
- if `failedStoriesCount > 0`, show a subtle warning/info note
- do not hardcode text; use string resources
- keep design-system color usage only

