# Architecture Notes to Enforce Throughout

## MVVM / SOLID / SSOT rules
- UI must not coordinate worker graphs directly
- ViewModel should delegate orchestration
- repository owns persistence semantics
- worker owns execution, not business policy
- planner/orchestrator/use case owns work graph creation
- final result truth should be clearly defined and consistent

## File size control
We should proactively expect refactors in:
- `TATTestViewModel.kt`
- possibly `TATSynthesisWorker.kt`
- possibly repository mapper files if they grow

If any touched file approaches ~260–280 lines, split immediately.

## Resource discipline
Any new user-facing text added in Phase 5 must go to:
- `app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml`

No hardcoded UI text or colors.

## Security discipline
During all phases:
- preserve Firestore auth/security rule compatibility
- avoid logging story bodies, prompts, or sensitive identifiers unnecessarily
- do not weaken repository boundaries
- do not introduce insecure global mutable coordination state

